+  //
+  //   astro.theme.preset  drives chrome/browser/oxy/ui/astro_color_mixer.cc,
+  //                       which owns the toolbar, the tab strip, the omnibox,
+  //                       the menus and the focus ring.
+  //   upstream's GM3 seed drives everything that mixer does NOT set -- the
+  //                       ui::kColorSys* tokens, and with them this side
+  //                       panel's own surfaces, the WebUI pages and the
+  //                       profile chooser.
+  //
+  // Writing only the first is what "the panel and the browser disagree" looks
+  // like: the chrome moves to the preset while the panel the user clicked in
+  // stays behind. Handing Chromium the preset's own Bloom `primary` as its
+  // seed makes it generate its Material palette from that colour, so the two
+  // agree without this file hand-mapping the forty-odd sys tokens.
+  //
+  // This is safe for the mixer, and not by luck: SetUserColorAndBrowserColor-
+  // Variant installs no theme supplier, it CLEARS one (ClearThemeData ->
+  // SwapThemeSupplier(nullptr)), so ColorProviderKey::custom_theme stays null
+  // and the Astro mixer -- which stands down only for an extension or
